s"}, {"contents": [{"content": "Quantifiers and Amounts", "type": "heading"}, {"content": "<ul><li>You use quantifiers to talk about the quantity or amount of something. </li> <li> Remember there are general and specific quantifiers.</li></ul>", "type": "describer"}, {"content": "{\"rows\":4,\"columns\":3,\"cells\":[\"\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"General Quantifiers\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Specific Quantifiers\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Count Nouns\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"All<br> Most<br> Many<br> Some<br> Any<br> A few<br> A lot of<br> A couple of<br> No\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"All of <br>  Most of<br> Many of<br> Some of<br> Any of<br> A few of<br> A lot of (the ... )<br> A couple of (the \u2026 )<br> None of\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" Non-Count Nouns\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" All<br> Some<br> Any<br> A little<br> Much<br> No\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"All of<br> Some of<br> Any of<br> A little<br> Much of\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" \\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" \\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" \\\"}\"],\"styles\":\" instruction_table_background intro_table_border\"}", "type": "table"}, {"content": "{\"rows\":13,\"columns\":2,\"cells\":[\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" Measurements (Nouns)\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" Amount\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" pound \\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" a little less than half a kilogram \\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"pint \\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"a little less than half a liter \\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" quart\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"a little less than one liter \\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"gallon \\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"about three and a half  liters\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"dozen\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"12 pieces\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" slice \\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"a piece cut from a whole \\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"case cup \\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"a box of 6, 12 or 24 bottles a little less than \\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"tin, jar, can\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"\u00bc of a liter containers \\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" a pinch / a dash \\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"a very small amount \\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"a teaspoon \\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"a small measuring spoon \\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"a tablespoon\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"a large measuring spoon\\\"}\"],\"styles\":\" intro_table_border instruction_table_background\"}", "type": "table"}, {"content": "Coat two pounds of pork shoulder with a spice rub. ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "Cook it with half a pound of sliced onions and half a pint of chicken broth.", "type": "example"}, {"content": " You can use half a cup of barbecue sauce to keep it moist.", "type": "example"}], "type": "learning_points"}, {"contents": [{"content": "to coat   ", "type": "name"}, {"content": "to cover food with a layer of sauce or other liquids", "type": "definition"}, {"content": " (verb)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: First, coat two pounds of pork shoulder with barbecue sauce.  ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn6le16ob05aud01", "type": "audio"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"content": " These are words you hear when you follow a recipe.", "type": "text"}], "type": "target_word_describer"}, {"contents": [{"content": "spice rub     ", "type": "name"}, {"content": "a mixture of spices used to coat food before it is cooked", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: Coat two pounds of pork shoulder with a spice rub of chili powder and cumin. ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn6le16ob05aud02", "type": "audio"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"content": "broth ", "type": "name"}, {"content": "light soup made of meat or vegetable stock ", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: Then, cook the meat with a pint of chicken broth.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn6le16ob05aud03", "type": "audio"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"content": "to shred      ", "type": "name"}, {"content": "to cut in tiny strips", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(verb)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: Shred the meat using two forks.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn6le16ob05aud04", "type": "audio"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"content": "to discard", "type": "name"}, {"content": "to get rid of something no longer useful ", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(verb)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: Discard any piece of fat from the meat. ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn6le16ob05aud05", "type": "audio"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"content": "bite-sized ", "type": "name"}, {"content": "small enough to be eaten in one mouthful ", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(adjective)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: Shred the meat to bite-sized pieces.  ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn6le16ob05aud06", "type": "audio"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"content": "moist  ", "type": "name"}, {"content": "slightly wet or damp", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(adjective)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: You can use half a cup of barbecue sauce to keep it moist.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn6le16ob05aud07", "type": "audio"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"content": "to feed a crowd ", "type": "name"}, {"content": "to make food for a lot of people ", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(expression)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: Pulled pork is enough to feed a crowd.  ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn6le16ob05aud08", "type": "audio"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"content": "leftovers ", "type": "name"}, {"content": "food left after a meal ", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: The best part is that you'll have leftovers for days!", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn6le16ob05aud09", "type": "audio"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"content": "Think of your favorite dish. Find out how to prepare it.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Go online or use a cookbook if you have one at home.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Write the steps involved in making the dish. Use quantities and amounts.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Read the recipe to your partner.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Write down your partner's recipe.", "type": "text"}], "type": "takeaway_extension"}, {"contents": [{"content": "I talk about how to prepare food.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "I use quantities and amounts.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "I write a recipe (8-10 lines) with steps and instructions.", "type": "text"}], "type": "takeaway_assessment"}], "labs": [{"stimuli": [{"template_override": 1, "contents": [{}], "_data": [], "id": 0, "type": "welcome"}, {"template_override": 1, "_data": [], "title": "", "type": "audio", "contents": [{"value": {"images": [{"image": "engenn6le16ob05re2img06.jpg", "time": "0", "id": 0, "text": ""}, {"image": "engenn6le16ob05re2img06.jpg", "time": "100", "id": 1, "text": "<span class=\"strong\">Vanessa</span>: Hey Bruce, I know you have a great pulled pork recipe. Do you mind sharing your secret?<br>\n<span class=\"strong\">Chef Bruce</span>: The great thing about this recipe is that you can just put all the ingredients in the cooker and walk away! I'm actually making some for tomorrow, too! The oven starts automatically at 6 a.m.!"}, {"image": "engenn6le16ob05re2img02.jpg", "time": "16000", "id": 2, "text": "<span class=\"strong\">Chef Bruce</span>: Just coat two pounds of pork shoulder with a spice rub of chili powder and cumin. Then, cook it on a bed of garlic and half a pound of sliced onions covered with half a pint of chicken broth. When you check on it six or eight hours later, you'll have juicy meat that's ready to be shredded and served with cornbread or potatoes."}, {"image": "engenn6le16ob05re2img01.jpg", "time": "34500", "id": 3, "text": "<span class=\"strong\">Vanessa</span>: How am I going to cut up the meat?<br>\n<span class=\"strong\">Chef Bruce</span>: Take 2 forks and shred the meat into bite-sized pieces, discarding any large pieces of fat. You can use half a cup of barbecue sauce to keep it moist. It's a versatile recipe, and it makes enough to feed a crowd! The best part is that you'll have leftovers for days!<br>\n<span class=\"strong\">Vanessa</span>: This sounds delicious! Thanks again!"}], "audiosrc": "engenn6le16ob05re2aud01", "coverimg": "engenn6le16ob05re2img06.jpg"}, "type": "slideshow"}], "id": 1}], "exercises": [{"template_override": 1, "_data": [{"contents": [{"content": " I can describe how to prepare food. ", "type": "Learning Outcomes"}, {"content": " I can talk about quantities and amounts. ", "type": "Learning Outcomes"}, {"content": " I can talk about future actions, plans and intentions. ", "